  ('2026-08-26-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'All: Send board packet to Adam by close of business Friday', 'All', 32),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'CONTRACTS UNDER LEGAL REVIEW — Both the Kindbridge and Evive contracts are with legal for final review. Brianne sent Matt a revised copy today with one correction caught. Matt has reviewed everything in detail — nothing controversial or expected to be a problem — but wants legal sign-off before signing. Pushing for a response within a day or so.', null, 1),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'EVIVE INTEGRATION TIMELINE — Sam at Evive is ready to go and has already populated the invoice, which will be the triggering event for the two-week integration. Brianne meeting with Dan tomorrow afternoon.', null, 2),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'LAUNCH DATE / BILLING TRIGGER — Dan asked whether a September 1 start date should be assumed. Brianne clarified his concern is billing-related: she negotiated a quarterly billing cycle (instead of a flat $90K upfront), so the effective/execution date matters for invoicing. Dan will still meet with the team ahead of time regardless — intro call for Tareq possible next week even if integration doesn''t start until September.', null, 3),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'ELISA UNAVAILABLE — Elisa texted that she''s en route to Atlanta for the TV show and won''t be on today''s call; available if anything is needed.', null, 4),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'ATLANTA DINNER RECAP — Michael had dinner with Adam Kaplan and the ~5 people who verbally committed to GCSG (Stephen Mel, William Acres, Eric Dolores, Charlie Koss, and others). All were inquisitive and positive about the council''s mission. Tareq also spoke with the group about GCSG and his background.', null, 5),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'SPELL OFF CAPITAL RAISE vs. GCSG — Adam is considering raising capital from the same donor pool for the "Spell Off" series, which has performed well above expectations. Plan under discussion: approach investors about Spell Off first, potentially requiring a matching GCSG donation as a condition of investment (similar to VC fund allocation practices). Michael to get clarity from the family office (Jeff) on strategy and sequencing.', null, 6),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'TAREQ''S $100K COMMITMENT — Tareq agreed to commit $100K to GCSG this week to keep momentum going, with more to follow later once the broader board/financial planning is in place. Michael to send wiring instructions, copying Brianne and Elisa. Adam also wants Tareq to meet with Jonathan Parente (GCSG''s lawyer) about deeper involvement.', null, 7),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'MEMBERSHIP / DUES MODEL — Brianne raised the idea of a membership program for industry operators (modeled on the Massachusetts Partnership for Responsible Gaming she helped set up in 2013) as a possible fundraising pivot, especially since two industry operators are leaving NCPG amid its funding controversy and may be looking for an alternative home for their RG dollars.', null, 8),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'NH COUNCIL / SEPT 22 KEYNOTE — Brianne has been invited to give a keynote (alongside Chris Christie) on September 22 for the New Hampshire Council for Responsible Gaming, a newly-forming council in a similar position to GCSG (industry-founder-backed, no state grants). Potential opportunity to compare notes on membership/fundraising models.', null, 9),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'DATA & REPORTING PLAN — Evive will begin providing usage data (portal visits, pathway chosen — cut back vs. abstain, time on app, self-reported demographics) within about a month of going live. Kindbridge will also begin reporting monthly call volume and conversion-to-treatment rates for the new Georgia number, similar to Brianne''s existing Florida program (Kindbridge Research Institute).', null, 10),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', '"DOLLARS TO LIVES SAVED" FRAMING — Tareq suggested mapping donation dollars to an approximate number of lives helped/saved as a compelling donor narrative. Brianne agreed data from Evive/Kindbridge will support this once baseline numbers come in.', null, 11),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'RUNNING GCSG LIKE A BUSINESS — Brianne emphasized deliberately not overspending or overhiring (e.g., not hiring a $120K+ full-time staffer prematurely) and using evidence/data to drive decisions on how much to raise and where to spend it, rather than picking an arbitrary large number.', null, 12),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'INDUSTRY PUSHBACK CASE STUDY — Brianne cited the Pennsylvania Gaming Control Board''s new RG regulations, where DraftKings, FanDuel, and Mohegan Sun submitted lengthy objections while Prize Picks (Wexler) took a more constructive stance — used as an example of why GCSG''s independence and credibility matter, and why unrestricted funds protect the Council''s ability to be critical of industry practices even while accepting industry money.', null, 13),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Kindbridge and Evive contracts sent for final legal review; Matt has no substantive concerns, awaiting legal sign-off before signature.', 'Agreed', 14),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Evive invoice triggers the start of the 2-week integration clock; not tied to a hard September 1 launch date.', 'Agreed', 15),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Tareq to wire an initial $100K commitment to GCSG this week.', 'Agreed', 16),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Spell Off investor outreach to proceed first, with GCSG donation matching/bundling as a likely condition — final approach pending family office input.', 'Agreed', 17),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Membership/dues fundraising model to be raised as a discussion item at the next GCSG board meeting.', 'Agreed', 18),
  ('2026-08-19-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Brianne to keynote the New Hampshire Council for Responsible Gaming event on September 22.', 'Agreed', 19),
