  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'TECHNICAL DIFFICULTIES — Michael experienced computer issues at the start of the call; Brianne joined late, still waiting on updates from Matt about the filming.', null, 1),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'SIGNATURE STILL PENDING — Tareq plans to attend the filming in Atlanta the next day. Brianne reiterated she is stuck until the Georgia Council for Safer Gaming gets the signature it needs from Matt; unclear whether it should go to Wexler or Kelly.', null, 2),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'INVESTOR OUTREACH — Michael has contacted five to seven potential investors for GCSG. Several have verbally committed, including Eric Dolorla and William Acres, who will attend the Atlanta dinner.', null, 3),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'FUNDING GOAL — Group discussed a target of raising $2M for GCSG, with potential to go higher; some investors open to larger commitments. Michael noted the amount raised may depend on the success of the initial spelling-series episodes (financial models discussed up to $5M–$10M).', null, 4),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'NETWORKING PLAN — Tareq Dowla and Adam Kaplan will assist Michael with introductions and networking with investors at the Atlanta dinner. Adam expressed confidence navigating the room.', null, 5),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'MESSAGING — Brianne emphasized the importance of clear, consistent messaging on GCSG''s core programs when speaking with investors: clinical treatment, digital intervention, and Gamban blocking software. (Note: transcript names these "Pinebridge" and "Avive" — likely auto-transcription variants of Kindbridge and Evive; verify before reusing in donor materials.)', null, 6),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'STRATEGIC SPENDING — Group discussed being strategic about how increased funding gets spent. Tareq requested a list of channels for expanded investment (e.g., workforce development, in-school curriculum, criminal justice, financial literacy). Brianne agreed to compile options.', null, 7),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'NCPG CRISIS WARNING — Brianne flagged a current crisis at the National Council on Problem Gambling: NCPG accepted a $2M donation from a controversial entity and is facing public and governmental backlash. She advised GCSG stay clear of NCPG and keep messaging mission-focused.', null, 8),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'GCSG will keep its distance from the National Council on Problem Gambling and keep messaging mission-focused amid NCPG''s funding controversy.', 'Agreed', 9),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Tareq and Adam will personally introduce themselves to prospective investors at the Atlanta dinner.', 'Agreed', 10),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'decision', 'Securing a signature for GCSG (from Wexler or Kelly) is the top priority — no further fundraising work proceeds until it''s in hand.', 'Agreed', 11),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Follow up with Matt to clarify who signs for GCSG (Wexler or Kelly) and confirm what''s needed before further work proceeds.', 'Brianne', 12),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'While at the Atlanta filming/dinner, ask attendees if someone would be willing to sign on behalf of GCSG.', 'Tareq', 13),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Send Matt a direct message stressing the urgency of getting signatures — ink on paper before more work is done.', 'Tareq', 14),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Next week, send the current GCSG funding deck plus clear funding instructions to investors who gave verbal commitments, after they''ve met Tareq and other key stakeholders.', 'Michael', 15),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Email a brief bio/background on role, mission, and current status of GCSG, with a bullet-point summary of the three priority measures, for Tareq to reference with investors.', 'Tareq', 16),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Compile and email a list of additional program opportunities/channels (expanded education, criminal justice, financial literacy, etc.) with rough cost estimates, to accompany donor outreach.', 'Brianne', 17),
  ('2026-08-11-gcsg-weekly', 'action', 'Once computer is working again, email the latest GCSG funding deck to the team ahead of the Atlanta dinner and filming.', 'Michael', 18),
  ('2026-08-04-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'KINDBRIDGE CONTRACT SIGNED — Elisa executed the Kindbridge contract. Helpline officially live as of this call. Services begin immediately under contract.', null, 1),
  ('2026-08-04-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'EVIVE CONTRACT SIGNED — Elisa also executed the Evive SOW. $25K wired by Kelly Ristler. 30-day deployment clock started. Evive goes live on georgiasafergaming.org by end of August.', null, 2),
  ('2026-08-04-gcsg-weekly', 'discussion', 'GAMBAN — Contract received from Matt Zarb-Cousin. Team reviewing. Expected to sign this week. Gamban subscriptions will be available to Georgians once executed.', null, 3),
